/* Lamp & Path Amplified: our own study rendering, the Berean Standard Bible (public domain) with the fuller
 * meaning of key Greek words in brackets, from Strong's dictionary (1890, public domain). Made with AI help. Book 46. */
window.Bible&&Bible._addVer("lpa",45,[["Paul, called [appointed, invited] to be an apostle [delegate, sent messenger] of Christ Jesus by the will of God, and our brother Sosthenes,","To the church [assembly, called-out ones] of God in Corinth, to those sanctified [made holy, consecrated] in Christ Jesus and called to be holy, together with all those everywhere who call on [invoke, appeal to] the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, their Lord and ours:","Grace [favor, graciousness] and peace [quietness, rest] to you from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.","I always thank [express gratitude to] my God for you because of the grace [favor, gift] He has given you in Christ Jesus.","For in Him you have been enriched [made wealthy] in every way, in all speech and all knowledge [knowing],","because our testimony [witness, evidence] about Christ was confirmed [established, made stable] in you.","Therefore you do not lack any spiritual gift as you eagerly await [fully expect, keep looking for] the revelation [disclosure, appearing] of our Lord Jesus Christ.","He will sustain [establish, confirm] you to the end, so that you will be blameless [unaccused, irreproachable] on the day of our Lord Jesus Christ.","God, who has called you into fellowship [partnership, participation, communion] with His Son Jesus Christ our Lord, is faithful [trustworthy, sure].","I appeal to [urge, exhort] you, brothers, in the name of our Lord Jesus Christ, that all of you agree together, so that there may be no divisions [splits, schisms] among you and that you may be united [thoroughly joined, restored] in mind and conviction.","My brothers, some from Chloe’s household have informed me that there are quarrels [strife, contentions] among you.","What I mean is this: Individuals among you are saying, “I follow Paul,” “I follow Apollos,” “I follow Cephas,” or “I follow Christ.”","Is Christ divided [split apart, apportioned]? Was Paul crucified for you? Were you baptized into the name of Paul?","I thank God that I did not baptize any of you except Crispus and Gaius,","so no one can say that you were baptized into my name.","Yes, I also baptized the household of Stephanas; beyond that I do not remember if I baptized anyone else.","For Christ did not send me to baptize, but to preach the gospel [announce good news], not with words of wisdom, lest the cross of Christ be emptied of its power [made void, neutralized].","For the message [word] of the cross is foolishness to those who are perishing [being destroyed], but to us who are being saved [delivered, made whole] it is the power of God.","For it is written: “I will destroy [fully destroy] the wisdom of the wise; the intelligence of the intelligent I will frustrate [set aside, bring to nothing].”","Where is the wise man? Where is the scribe? Where is the philosopher [disputer, debater] of this age? Has not God made foolish [made insipid] the wisdom of the world?","For since in the wisdom of God the world through its wisdom did not know [perceive] Him, God was pleased [thought it good] through the foolishness of what was preached to save those who believe [continually believe, trust].","Jews demand [keep asking for] signs and Greeks search for [keep seeking] wisdom,","but we preach [herald, proclaim] Christ crucified, a stumbling block [trap, offense] to Jews and foolishness to Gentiles,","but to those who are called [invited, appointed], both Jews and Greeks, Christ the power [might, ability] of God and the wisdom of God.","For the foolishness of God is wiser than man’s wisdom, and the weakness of God is stronger than man’s strength.","Brothers, consider [look at, regard] the time of your calling [invitation]: Not many of you were wise by human standards; not many were powerful; not many were of noble birth [well born].","But God chose [selected] the foolish things of the world to shame [disgrace, put to shame] the wise; God chose the weak things of the world to shame the strong.","He chose the lowly [ignoble, base] and despised [set at nothing] things of the world, and the things that are not, to nullify [render idle, abolish] the things that are,","so that no one may boast [vaunt, glory] in His presence.","It is because of Him that you are in Christ Jesus, who has become for us wisdom from God: our righteousness [justification, equity], holiness [sanctification, purity], and redemption [full ransom, deliverance].","Therefore, as it is written: “Let him who boasts boast in [glory, rejoice] the Lord.”"],["When I came to you, brothers, I did not come with eloquence [superiority, excellency] or wisdom as I proclaimed [kept declaring] to you the testimony [witness, evidence] about God.","For I resolved [determined, decided] to know nothing while I was with you except Jesus Christ and Him crucified [and remains so].","I came to you in weakness [feebleness, frailty] and fear [alarm], and with much trembling.","My message and my preaching were not with persuasive [enticing] words of wisdom, but with a demonstration [manifestation, proof] of the Spirit’s power,","so that your faith [belief, conviction, trust] would not rest on men’s wisdom, but on God’s power.","Among the mature [complete, of full age], however, we speak a message of wisdom—but not the wisdom of this age or of the rulers of this age, who are coming to nothing [being rendered idle, abolished].","No, we speak of the mysterious [secret] and hidden wisdom of God, which He destined [predetermined, ordained beforehand] for our glory [honor, dignity] before time began.","None of the rulers of this age understood [perceived, knew] it. For if they had, they would not have crucified the Lord of glory.","Rather, as it is written: “No eye has seen, no ear has heard, no heart has imagined, what God has prepared [made ready, provided] for those who love [continually love] Him.”","But God has revealed [uncovered, disclosed] it to us by the Spirit. The Spirit searches [keeps investigating] all things, even the deep things [depths, profundities] of God.","For who among men knows [is aware of] the thoughts of man except his own spirit within him? So too, no one knows the thoughts of God except the Spirit of God.","We have not received [taken, accepted] the spirit of the world, but the Spirit who is from God, that we may understand what God has freely given [granted as a favor] us.","And this is what we speak, not in words taught [instructed] us by human wisdom, but in words taught by the Spirit, expressing [combining, comparing] spiritual truths in spiritual words.","The natural [unspiritual, merely animate] man does not accept [receive] the things that come from the Spirit of God. For they are foolishness to him, and he cannot understand them, because they are spiritually discerned [examined, investigated].","The spiritual man judges [examines, discerns] all things, but he himself is not subject to anyone’s judgment.","“For who has known the mind [intellect, understanding] of the Lord, so as to instruct Him?” But we have the mind of Christ."],["Brothers, I could not address you as spiritual [non-carnal], but as worldly [fleshly, carnal]—as infants [babes, little children] in Christ.","I gave you milk, not solid food [meat], for you were not yet ready for solid food. In fact, you are still not ready,","for you are still worldly [fleshly, carnal]. For since there is jealousy [envy, rivalry] and dissension among you, are you not worldly? Are you not walking [conducting yourselves] in the way of man?","For when one of you says, “I follow Paul,” and another, “I follow Apollos,” are you not mere men [fleshly, carnal]?","What then is Apollos? And what is Paul? They are servants [attendants, ministers] through whom you believed [put your faith], as the Lord has assigned to each his role.","I planted the seed and Apollos watered it, but God made it grow [kept giving the increase].","So neither he who plants nor he who waters is anything, but only God, who makes things grow [continually gives the increase].","He who plants and he who waters are one in purpose, and each will be rewarded [paid, given wages] according to his own labor [toil, weariness].","For we are God’s fellow workers [co-laborers]; you are God’s field [cultivated farm], God’s building [structure].","By the grace [favor, gift] God has given me, I laid a foundation as an expert builder [master builder, architect], and someone else is building on it. But each one must be careful [look, take heed] how he builds.","For no one can lay a foundation other than the one already laid [set, appointed], which is Jesus Christ.","If anyone builds on this foundation using gold, silver, precious stones, wood, hay, or straw,","his workmanship will be evident [apparent, manifest], because the Day will bring it to light. It will be revealed [disclosed, uncovered] with fire, and the fire will prove [test, examine] the quality of each man’s work.","If what he has built survives [remains, endures], he will receive a reward [wages, pay].","If it is burned up, he will suffer loss [experience damage]. He himself will be saved [delivered, preserved], but only as if through the flames.","Do you not know that you yourselves are God’s temple [sanctuary, shrine], and that God’s Spirit dwells [resides, makes His home] in you?","If anyone destroys [corrupts, defiles] God’s temple, God will destroy him; for God’s temple is holy [sacred, consecrated], and you are that temple.","Let no one deceive [beguile, fully mislead] himself. If any of you thinks he is wise in this age, he should become a fool, so that he may become wise.","For the wisdom of this world is foolishness [absurdity, silliness] in God’s sight. As it is written: “He catches [grasps, entraps] the wise in their craftiness [trickery, cunning].”","And again, “The Lord knows that the thoughts [reasonings] of the wise are futile [empty, vain, profitless].”","Therefore, stop boasting [vaunting, glorying] in men. All things are yours,","whether Paul or Apollos or Cephas or the world or life [life-time] or death or the present [what is at hand] or the future. All of them belong to you,","and you belong to Christ, and Christ belongs to God."],["So then, men ought to regard [account, esteem] us as servants [assistants, officers] of Christ and stewards [household managers] of the mysteries of God.","Now it is required of stewards that they be found faithful [trustworthy, true].","I care very little, however, if I am judged [examined, scrutinized] by you or by any human court. In fact, I do not even judge myself.","My conscience is clear [aware of nothing against me], but that does not vindicate [justify, declare innocent] me. It is the Lord who judges [examines] me.","Therefore judge nothing before the appointed time [proper season]; wait until the Lord comes. He will bring to light [illuminate, enlighten] what is hidden in darkness and will expose the motives [purposes, counsels] of men’s hearts. At that time each will receive his praise from God.","Brothers, I have applied [transferred] these things to myself and Apollos for your benefit, so that you may learn from us not to go beyond what is written. Then you will not take pride [be puffed up] in one man over another.","For who makes you so superior [different, distinguished]? What do you have that you did not receive? And if you did receive it, why do you boast [vaunt, glory] as though you did not?","Already you have all you want [been filled, satisfied]. Already you have become rich. Without us, you have become kings [reigned, ruled]. How I wish you really were kings, so that we might be kings with you!","For it seems to me that God has displayed [exhibited, set forth] us apostles at the end of the procession, like prisoners appointed for death [doomed to death]. We have become a spectacle [theatre, public show] to the whole world, to angels as well as to men.","We are fools for Christ, but you are wise [thoughtful, sensible] in Christ. We are weak, but you are strong. You are honored [glorious, splendid], but we are dishonored [without honor].","To this very hour we are hungry and thirsty, we are poorly clothed, we are brutally treated [struck with fists, buffeted], we are homeless [without settled dwelling].","We work hard [toil to weariness] with our own hands. When we are vilified [reviled, reproached], we bless; when we are persecuted, we endure [bear with, put up with] it;","when we are slandered [defamed, reviled], we answer gently [appeal, entreat]. Up to this moment we have become the scum [offscouring, scrapings] of the earth, the refuse of the world.","I am not writing this to shame you, but to warn [admonish, caution] you as my beloved [dearly loved] children.","Even if you have ten thousand guardians [instructors, tutors] in Christ, you do not have many fathers; for in Christ Jesus I became your father [begot you] through the gospel.","Therefore I urge [exhort, beseech] you to imitate [become imitators of] me.","That is why I have sent you Timothy, my beloved and faithful [trustworthy] child in the Lord. He will remind [bring to mind] you of my way of life [ways, road] in Christ Jesus, which is exactly what I teach everywhere in every church.","Some of you have become arrogant [puffed up, inflated], as if I were not coming to you.","But I will come to you shortly, if the Lord is willing, and then I will find out not only what these arrogant [puffed up] people are saying, but what power [might, ability] they have.","For the kingdom [rule, reign] of God is not a matter of talk but of power [might, ability].","Which do you prefer? Shall I come to you with a rod, or in love [affection, benevolence] and with a gentle [meek, mild] spirit?"],["It is actually reported that there is sexual immorality [fornication, harlotry] among you, and of a kind that is intolerable even among pagans [Gentiles, nations]: A man has his father’s wife.","And you are proud [puffed up, inflated]! Shouldn’t you rather have been stricken with grief [mourned, grieved] and have removed from your fellowship the man who did this?","Although I am absent from you in body, I am present with you in spirit, and I have already pronounced judgment [judged, decided, condemned] on the one who did this, just as if I were present.","When you are assembled [gathered together] in the name of our Lord Jesus and I am with you in spirit, along with the power [might, ability] of the Lord Jesus,","hand this man over [deliver, surrender] to Satan for the destruction [ruin] of the flesh, so that his spirit may be saved [delivered, rescued] on the Day of the Lord.","Your boasting [glorying] is not good. Do you not know that a little leaven works through [leavens, ferments] the whole batch of dough?","Get rid of [cleanse thoroughly, purge] the old [worn out] leaven, that you may be a new unleavened batch, as you really are. For Christ, our Passover lamb, has been sacrificed [slain].","Therefore let us keep the feast [continually observe the festival], not with the old bread, leavened with malice [badness, depravity] and wickedness, but with the unleavened bread of sincerity [clearness, purity] and of truth.","I wrote you in my letter not to associate [mix together, keep company] with sexually immoral people.","I was not including the sexually immoral of this world, or the greedy [covetous, eager for gain] and swindlers [extortioners, rapacious], or idolaters. In that case you would have to leave this world.","But now I am writing you not to associate [keep company] with anyone who claims to be a brother but is sexually immoral or greedy, an idolater or a verbal abuser [reviler, railer], a drunkard or a swindler. With such a man do not even eat.","What business of mine is it to judge [try, decide] those outside the church? Are you not to judge those inside?","God will judge those outside. “Expel [remove, put away] the wicked [evil, malicious] man from among you.”"],["If any of you has a grievance [matter, affair] against another, how dare he go to law before the unrighteous [unjust] instead of before the saints [holy ones]!","Do you not know that the saints [holy ones] will judge the world? And if you are to judge the world, are you not competent [fit, worthy] to judge trivial cases [smallest matters]?","Do you not know that we will judge angels? How much more the things of this life [matters of present existence]!","So if you need to settle everyday matters, do you appoint as judges those of no standing [least esteemed, set at nothing] in the church [assembly]?","I say this to your shame [confusion]. Is there really no one among you wise enough to arbitrate [judge, decide] between his brothers?","Instead, one brother goes to law against another, and this in front of unbelievers [those without faith]!","The very fact that you have lawsuits among you means that you are thoroughly defeated [at a loss, failing] already. Why not rather be wronged [treated unjustly]? Why not rather be cheated [defrauded]?","Instead, you yourselves cheat [defraud] and do wrong [act unjustly], even against your own brothers!","Do you not know that the wicked [unrighteous, unjust] will not inherit [be heirs of] the kingdom of God? Do not be deceived [led astray]: Neither the sexually immoral, nor idolaters, nor adulterers, nor men who submit to or perform homosexual acts,","nor thieves, nor the greedy [covetous], nor drunkards, nor verbal abusers, nor swindlers [extortioners], will inherit the kingdom of God.","And that is what some of you were. But you were washed [washed fully, cleansed], you were sanctified [made holy, consecrated], you were justified [declared righteous], in the name of the Lord Jesus Christ and by the Spirit of our God.","“Everything is permissible [lawful] for me,” but not everything is beneficial [profitable, expedient]. “Everything is permissible for me,” but I will not be mastered [brought under the power] by anything.","“Food for the stomach and the stomach for food,” but God will destroy [render idle, abolish] them both. The body is not intended for sexual immorality [fornication], but for the Lord, and the Lord for the body.","By His power God raised the Lord from the dead, and He will raise us [rouse fully, resurrect] also.","Do you not know that your bodies are members [limbs, parts] of Christ? Shall I then take the members of Christ and unite them with a prostitute? Never!","Or don’t you know that he who unites himself [joins, cleaves] with a prostitute is one with her in body? For it is said, “The two will become one flesh.”","But he who unites himself [joins, cleaves] with the Lord is one with Him in spirit.","Flee [keep running away, shun] from sexual immorality. Every other sin [sinful deed] a man can commit is outside his body, but he who sins sexually sins against [misses the mark] his own body.","Do you not know that your body is a temple [shrine, sanctuary] of the Holy Spirit who is in you, whom you have received [have, hold] from God? You are not your own;","you were bought [purchased, redeemed] at a price [value]. Therefore glorify [honor, magnify] God with your body."],["Now for the matters you wrote about: It is good [fine, well] to abstain from sexual relations.","But because there is so much sexual immorality [fornication], each man should have his own wife, and each woman her own husband.","The husband should fulfill his marital duty [what is owed, good will] to his wife, and likewise the wife to her husband.","The wife does not have authority [power, control] over her own body, but the husband. Likewise the husband does not have authority over his own body, but the wife.","Do not deprive [defraud] each other, except by mutual consent and for a time, so you may devote yourselves [be at leisure, give yourselves] to prayer. Then come together again, so that Satan will not tempt you through your lack of self-control [want of self-restraint].","I say this as a concession [permission], not as a command [commandment, injunction].","I wish that all men were as I am. But each man has his own gift [free gift, gracious endowment] from God; one has this gift, another has that.","Now to the unmarried and widows I say this: It is good for them to remain [continue, abide] unmarried, as I am.","But if they cannot control themselves [exercise self-restraint], let them marry. For it is better to marry than to burn with passion [be set on fire].","To the married I give this command [charge, instruction] (not I, but the Lord): A wife must not separate [depart] from her husband.","But if she does, she must remain unmarried or else be reconciled [brought back into harmony] to her husband. And a husband must not divorce his wife.","To the rest I say this (I, not the Lord): If a brother has an unbelieving [faithless, without faith] wife and she is willing [consents, is pleased] to live with him, he must not divorce her.","And if a woman has an unbelieving [faithless] husband and he is willing [consents, is pleased] to live with her, she must not divorce him.","For the unbelieving husband is sanctified [made holy, consecrated] through his believing wife, and the unbelieving wife is sanctified through her believing husband. Otherwise your children would be unclean [impure], but now they are holy [sacred, pure].","But if the unbeliever leaves, let him go. The believing brother or sister is not bound [enslaved, under bondage] in such cases. God has called you to live in peace [quietness, rest].","How do you know, wife, whether you will save [deliver, make whole] your husband? Or how do you know, husband, whether you will save your wife?","Regardless, each one should lead the life [walk, conduct himself] that the Lord has assigned [apportioned, distributed] to him and to which God has called him. This is what I prescribe [order, ordain] in all the churches.","Was a man already circumcised when he was called? He should not become uncircumcised. Was a man still uncircumcised when called? He should not be circumcised.","Circumcision is nothing and uncircumcision is nothing. Keeping [observing] God’s commandments [injunctions, precepts] is what counts.","Each one should remain [abide, continue] in the situation [calling] he was in when he was called.","Were you a slave when you were called? Do not let it concern [be a care to] you—but if you can gain your freedom, take the opportunity [rather make use].","For he who was a slave when he was called by the Lord is the Lord’s freedman [one set free]. Conversely, he who was a free man when he was called is Christ’s slave.","You were bought [purchased, redeemed] at a price; do not become slaves of men.","Brothers, each one should remain [abide, continue] in the situation he was in when God called him.","Now about virgins, I have no command from the Lord, but I give a judgment [opinion, advice] as one who by the Lord’s mercy [compassion, pity] is trustworthy [faithful].","Because of the present [impending, at hand] crisis [distress, constraint], I think it is good for a man to remain as he is.","Are you committed [bound, tied] to a wife? Do not seek to be released [loosed]. Are you free of commitment? Do not look for a wife.","But if you do marry, you have not sinned [missed the mark]. And if a virgin marries, she has not sinned. But those who marry will face troubles [pressure, affliction] in this life, and I want to spare [forbear] you this.","What I am saying, brothers, is that the time is short [drawn together, shortened]. From now on those who have wives should live as if they had none;","those who weep [wail, sob], as if they did not; those who are joyful [glad, rejoicing], as if they were not; those who make a purchase, as if they had nothing;","and those who use the things of this world, as if not dependent on [overusing, misusing] them. For this world in its present form [outward fashion] is passing away [departing].","I want you to be free from concern [without anxiety]. The unmarried man is concerned [anxious, careful] about the work of the Lord, how he can please [be agreeable to] the Lord.","But the married man is concerned [anxious, careful] about the affairs of this world, how he can please his wife,","and his interests are divided [split, apportioned]. The unmarried woman or virgin is concerned about the work of the Lord, how she can be holy [sacred, consecrated] in both body and spirit. But the married woman is concerned about the affairs of this world, how she can please her husband.","I am saying this for your own good, not to restrict [put a noose upon] you, but in order to promote proper decorum [comeliness, honorable order] and undivided [without distraction] devotion to the Lord.","However, if someone thinks he is acting inappropriately [behaving in an unseemly way] toward his betrothed, and if she is beyond her youth [past her prime] and they ought to marry, let him do as he wishes; he is not sinning; they should get married.","But the man who is firmly established [stands steadfast, settled] in his heart and under no constraint [necessity], with control [authority, power] over his will and resolve in his heart not to marry the virgin, he will do well.","So then, he who marries the virgin does well, but he who does not marry her does even better.","A wife is bound [tied, bound by law] to her husband as long as he lives. But if her husband dies [falls asleep], she is free [at liberty] to marry anyone she wishes, as long as he belongs to the Lord.","In my judgment [opinion], however, she is happier [more blessed, more fortunate] if she remains as she is. And I think that I too have the Spirit of God."],["Now about food sacrificed to idols: We know that we all have knowledge [knowing]. Knowledge puffs up [inflates with pride], but love builds up [edifies].","The one who thinks [supposes] he knows something does not yet know [perceive, understand] as he ought to know.","But the one who loves [continually loves] God is known [is known and remains so] by God.","So about eating food sacrificed to idol [image for worship]s: We know that an idol is nothing at all in the world, and that there is no God but one.","For even if there are so-called gods, whether in heaven or on earth (as there are many so-called gods and lords),","yet for us there is but one God, the Father, from whom all things came and for whom we exist. And there is but one Lord, Jesus Christ, through whom all things came and through whom we exist.","But not everyone has this knowledge. Some people are still so accustomed [used to] to idols that they eat such food as if it were sacrificed to an idol. And since their conscience [moral consciousness] is weak, it is defiled [soiled].","But food does not bring us closer [present, commend] to God: We are no worse if we do not eat, and no better if we do.","Be careful [keep on watching, beware], however, that your freedom [liberty, right] does not become a stumbling block [occasion of stumbling] to the weak.","For if someone with a weak conscience sees you who are well informed [having knowledge] eating in an idol’s temple, will he not be encouraged [built up, emboldened] to eat food sacrificed to idols?","So this weak brother, for whom Christ died, is destroyed [ruined, lost] by your knowledge.","By sinning against your brothers in this way and wounding [striking, beating] their weak [feeble] conscience, you sin [miss the mark] against Christ.","Therefore, if what I eat causes my brother to stumble [trip up, be offended], I will never eat meat again, so that I will not cause him to stumble."],["Am I not free [at liberty, unrestrained]? Am I not an apostle [sent messenger, delegate]? Have I not seen Jesus our Lord? Are you yourselves not my workmanship [work, labor] in the Lord?","Even if I am not an apostle to others, surely I am to you. For you are the seal [signet] of my apostleship [commission] in the Lord.","This is my defense [plea, answer] to those who scrutinize [examine, question] me:","Have we no right [authority, privilege] to food and to drink?","Have we no right [authority, privilege] to take along [lead about as a companion] a believing wife, as do the other apostles and the Lord’s brothers and Cephas?","Or are Barnabas and I the only apostles who must work for a living [toil, labor]?","Who serves as a soldier [goes to war] at his own expense [wages, rations]? Who plants a vineyard and does not eat of its fruit? Who tends [shepherds] a flock and does not drink of its milk?","Do I say this from a human perspective? Doesn’t the Law say the same thing?","For it is written in the Law of Moses: “Do not muzzle an ox while it is treading out the grain.” Is it about oxen that God is concerned [takes care]?","Isn’t He actually speaking on our behalf? Indeed, this was written for us, because when the plowman plows and the thresher threshes, they should also expect [hope, confident expectation] to share [participate, partake] in the harvest.","If we have sown spiritual [non-carnal] seed among you, is it too much for us to reap [harvest] a material [fleshly, bodily] harvest from you?","If others have this right [authority, privilege] to your support, shouldn’t we have it all the more? But we did not exercise this right. Instead, we put up with [bear, endure] anything rather than hinder [hindrance] the gospel of Christ.","Do you not know that those who work in the temple eat of its food, and those who serve [attend, wait] at the altar partake [share jointly] of its offerings?","In the same way, the Lord has prescribed [ordained, commanded] that those who preach [proclaim, declare] the gospel should receive their living from the gospel.","But I have not used any of these rights. And I am not writing this to suggest that something be done for me. Indeed, I would rather die than let anyone nullify [make empty, make void] my boast [glorying, rejoicing].","Yet when I preach the gospel [announce good news], I have no reason to boast, because I am obligated [under necessity, constrained] to preach. Woe to me if I do not preach the gospel!","If my preaching is voluntary [willing], I have a reward [pay, wages]. But if it is not voluntary, I am still entrusted with a responsibility [stewardship].","What then is my reward? That in preaching the gospel I may offer it free of charge [without expense], and so not use up [overuse, misuse] my rights in preaching it.","Though I am free of obligation to anyone, I make myself a slave [enslave myself] to everyone, to win [gain] as many as possible.","To the Jews I became like a Jew, to win [gain] the Jews. To those under the law I became like one under the law (though I myself am not under the law), to win those under the law.","To those without the law [lawless, not subject to law] I became like one without the law (though I am not outside the law of God but am under the law of Christ [legal, subject]), to win those without the law.","To the weak [feeble, without strength] I became weak, to win the weak. I have become all things to all people so that by all possible means I might save [deliver, rescue] some.","I do all this for the sake of the gospel, so that I may share [co-participant, partner] in its blessings.","Do you not know that in a race [stadium] all the runners run, but only one receives the prize [award]? Run in such a way as to take [seize, attain] the prize.","Everyone who competes [strives, struggles] in the games trains with strict discipline [exercises self-restraint]. They do it for a crown that is perishable, but we do it for a crown that is imperishable [incorruptible, undecaying].","Therefore I do not run aimlessly [uncertainly]; I do not fight [box] like I am beating the air.","No, I discipline [strike, keep under] my body and make it my slave [bring into subjection], so that after I have preached to others, I myself will not be disqualified [rejected, unapproved]."],["I do not want you to be unaware [ignorant, without knowledge], brothers, that our forefathers were all under the cloud, and that they all passed through the sea.","They were all baptized [immersed] into Moses in the cloud and in the sea.","They all ate the same spiritual [non-carnal] food","and drank the same spiritual drink; for they drank from the spiritual rock that accompanied [followed] them, and that rock was Christ.","Nevertheless, God was not pleased [well pleased, approving] with most of them, for they were struck down [overthrown, laid low] in the wilderness.","These things took place as examples [patterns, figures] to keep us from craving [longing for, lusting after] evil things as they did.","Do not be idolaters [image-worshipers], as some of them were. As it is written: “The people sat down to eat and to drink, and got up to indulge in revelry [play, sport].”","We should not commit sexual immorality [commit fornication], as some of them did, and in one day twenty-three thousand of them died.","We should not test [test thoroughly, tempt] Christ, as some of them did, and were killed [destroyed] by snakes.","And do not complain [keep grumbling, murmur], as some of them did, and were killed by the destroying angel [destroyer, ruiner].","Now these things happened to them as examples [patterns, types] and were written down as warnings [admonition, mild rebuke] for us, on whom the fulfillment [end, goal] of the ages has come.","So the one who thinks he is standing firm [established, stands fast] should be careful [keep watching, beware] not to fall.","No temptation [testing, trial] has seized you except what is common to man. And God is faithful [trustworthy, sure]; He will not let you be tempted beyond what you can bear. But when you are tempted, He will also provide an escape [way out, exit], so that you can stand up under it.","Therefore, my beloved [dearly loved], flee [keep running away, shun] from idolatry [image-worship].","I speak to reasonable [thoughtful, sensible] people; judge [decide] for yourselves what I say.","Is not the cup of blessing [commendation, praise] that we bless a participation [fellowship, communion, sharing] in the blood of Christ? And is not the bread that we break a participation in the body of Christ?","Because there is one loaf, we who are many are one body; for we all partake [share, participate] of the one loaf.","Consider the people of Israel: Are not those who eat the sacrifices fellow partakers [sharers, partners] in the altar?","Am I suggesting, then, that food sacrificed to an idol is anything, or that an idol is anything?","No, but the sacrifices of pagans are offered to demons, not to God. And I do not want you to be participants [sharers, partners] with demons.","You cannot drink the cup of the Lord and the cup of demons too; you cannot partake [share, participate] in the table of the Lord and the table of demons too.","Are we trying to provoke the Lord to jealousy [stir to rivalry]? Are we stronger [mightier] than He?","“Everything is permissible [lawful],” but not everything is beneficial [profitable, expedient]. “Everything is permissible,” but not everything is edifying [building up].","No one should seek [keep seeking] his own good, but the good of others.","Eat anything sold in the meat market without raising questions [examining, inquiring] of conscience [moral consciousness],","for, “The earth is the Lord’s, and the fullness [what fills it, completeness] thereof.”","If an unbeliever [one without faith] invites you to a meal and you want to go, eat anything set before you without raising questions of conscience.","But if someone tells you, “This food was offered to idols,” then do not eat it, for the sake of the one who told you and for the sake of conscience—","the other one’s conscience, I mean, not your own. For why should my freedom [liberty] be determined [judged] by someone else’s conscience?","If I partake in the meal with thankfulness [grace, gratitude], why am I denounced [reviled, defamed] because of that for which I give thanks [express gratitude]?","So whether you eat or drink or whatever you do, do it all to the glory [honor, praise] of God.","Do not become a stumbling block [cause of offense], whether to Jews or Greeks or the church [assembly] of God—","as I also try to please [be agreeable to] everyone in all I do. For I am not seeking my own good [profit, advantage], but the good of many, that they may be saved [delivered, made whole]."],["You are to imitate me [be imitators of me], just as I imitate Christ.","Now I commend [praise] you for remembering me in everything and for maintaining [holding fast] the traditions [precepts handed down], just as I passed them on to you.","But I want you to understand [know] that the head of every man is Christ, and the head of the woman is man, and the head of Christ is God.","Every man who prays or prophesies [speaks under inspiration] with his head covered dishonors [disgraces, puts to shame] his head.","And every woman who prays or prophesies with her head uncovered [unveiled] dishonors [disgraces] her head, for it is just as if her head were shaved.","If a woman does not cover [veil wholly] her head, she should have her hair cut off. And if it is shameful [base, disgraceful] for a woman to have her hair cut or shaved off, she should cover her head.","A man ought [is bound] not to cover his head, since he is the image [likeness] and glory [honor, dignity] of God; but the woman is the glory of man.","For man did not come from woman, but woman from man.","Neither was man created [formed, made] for woman, but woman for man.","For this reason a woman ought to have a sign of authority [power, right] on her head, because of the angels.","In the Lord, however, woman is not independent of [apart from] man, nor is man independent of woman.","For just as woman came from man, so also man is born of woman. But everything comes from God.","Judge for yourselves: Is it proper [fitting, becoming] for a woman to pray to God with her head uncovered [unveiled]?","Doesn’t nature [natural order] itself teach you that if a man has long hair, it is a disgrace [dishonor, shame] to him,","but that if a woman has long hair, it is her glory [honor]? For long hair is given to her as a covering [veil, mantle].","If anyone is inclined to dispute [be contentious] this, we have no other practice [custom], nor do the churches [assemblies] of God.","In the following instructions [charge, commands] I have no praise [commendation] to offer, because your gatherings do more harm than good.","First of all, I hear that when you come together as a church, there are divisions [splits, schisms] among you, and in part I believe it.","And indeed, there must be differences [factions, parties] among you to show [make manifest] which of you are approved [tested and accepted].","Now then, when you come together, it is not the Lord’s Supper [evening meal] you eat.","For as you eat, each of you goes ahead [takes before others] without sharing his meal. While one remains hungry, another gets drunk.","Don’t you have your own homes in which to eat and drink? Or do you despise [disesteem, think little of] the church of God and humiliate [shame, disgrace] those who have nothing? What can I say to you? Shall I praise you for this? No, I will not!","For I received [took to myself] from the Lord what I also passed on [delivered, transmitted] to you: The Lord Jesus, on the night He was betrayed, took bread,","and when He had given thanks [expressed gratitude], He broke it and said, “This is My body, which is for you; do this in remembrance [recollection, memorial] of Me.”","In the same way, after supper He took the cup, saying, “This cup is the new [fresh] covenant [testament, binding agreement] in My blood; do this, as often as you drink it, in remembrance of Me.”","For as often as you eat this bread and drink this cup, you proclaim [declare, keep announcing] the Lord’s death until He comes.","Therefore, whoever eats the bread or drinks the cup of the Lord in an unworthy manner [irreverently] will be guilty [liable, answerable] of sinning against the body and blood of the Lord.","Each one must examine [test, prove] himself before he eats of the bread and drinks of the cup.","For anyone who eats and drinks without recognizing [discerning] the body eats and drinks judgment [condemnation, sentence] on himself.","That is why many among you are weak [without strength, feeble] and sick [infirm], and a number of you have fallen asleep [died].","Now if we judged ourselves [discerned, examined] properly, we would not come under judgment.","But when we are judged by the Lord, we are being disciplined [trained as children, chastened] so that we will not be condemned [sentenced] with the world.","So, my brothers, when you come together to eat, wait for [expect] one another.","If anyone is hungry, he should eat at home, so that when you come together it will not result in judgment [condemnation]. And when I come, I will give instructions [set in order] about the remaining matters."],["Now about spiritual gifts [things of the Spirit, supernatural], brothers, I do not want you to be uninformed [without understanding, ignorant].","You know that when you were pagans, you were influenced and led astray [carried away, taken off] to mute [voiceless, without meaning] idols.","Therefore I inform [make known, declare] you that no one who is speaking by the Spirit of God says, “Jesus be cursed [under a ban, accursed],” and no one can say, “Jesus is Lord [Master, supreme in authority],” except by the Holy Spirit.","There are different gifts [free gifts of grace], but the same Spirit.","There are different ministries [services, attendance as servants], but the same Lord.","There are different ways of working, but the same God works [is active, effectual] all things in all people.","Now to each one the manifestation [expression, exhibition, bestowment] of the Spirit is given for the common good [what is profitable, benefit].","To one there is given through the Spirit the message of wisdom, to another the message of knowledge [knowing] by the same Spirit,","to another faith [conviction, assurance] by the same Spirit, to another gifts of healing [cures] by that one Spirit,","to another the working of miracles [mighty power, mighty deeds], to another prophecy, to another distinguishing [discerning] between spirits, to another speaking in various tongues, and to still another the interpretation [translation] of tongues.","All these are the work of one and the same Spirit, who apportions [distributes, divides] them to each one as He determines [wills, intends].","The body is a unit, though it is composed of many parts [members, limbs]. And although its parts are many, they all form one body. So it is with Christ.","For in one Spirit we were all baptized [immersed] into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, slave or free, and we were all given one Spirit to drink [be watered].","For the body does not consist of one part, but of many.","If the foot should say, “Because I am not a hand, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.","And if the ear should say, “Because I am not an eye, I do not belong to the body,” that would not make it any less a part of the body.","If the whole body were an eye, where would the sense of hearing be? If the whole body were an ear, where would the sense of smell be?","But in fact, God has arranged [placed, set, appointed] the members of the body, every one of them, according to His design [will, choice].","If they were all one part, where would the body be?","As it is, there are many parts, but one body.","The eye cannot say to the hand, “I do not need you.” Nor can the head say to the feet, “I do not need you.”","On the contrary, the parts of the body that seem to be weaker are indispensable [necessary, needful],","and the parts we consider less honorable, we treat with greater honor [value, preciousness]. And our unpresentable parts are treated with special modesty [seemliness, decorum],","whereas our presentable parts have no such need. But God has composed [mixed together, combined] the body and has given greater honor to the parts that lacked [fell short, came behind] it,","so that there should be no division [split, rent, schism] in the body, but that its members should have mutual concern [care, anxious thought] for one another.","If one part suffers, every part suffers with [shares the pain of] it; if one part is honored [glorified, esteemed], every part rejoices with [shares the gladness of] it.","Now you are the body of Christ, and each of you is a member [limb, part] of it.","And in the church [assembly, called-out ones] God has appointed first of all apostles, second prophets, third teachers, then workers of miracles, and those with gifts of healing, helping [relief, help], administration [guidance, directorship], and various tongues.","Are all apostles? Are all prophets? Are all teachers? Do all work miracles?","Do all have gifts of healing? Do all speak in tongues? Do all interpret [explain thoroughly]?","But eagerly desire [keep on earnestly desiring, covet] the greater gifts. And now I will show you the most excellent [supreme, exceeding] way."],["If I speak in the tongues of men and of angels, but have not love [affection, benevolence], I am only a ringing [loudly reverberating, roaring] gong or a clanging [clashing, wailing] cymbal.","If I have the gift of prophecy and can fathom all mysteries [secrets] and all knowledge, and if I have absolute faith [conviction, assurance] so as to move mountains, but have not love, I am nothing [not even one thing].","If I give all I possess to the poor and exult in the surrender [yielding up, delivering] of my body, but have not love, I gain [am profited, benefited] nothing.","Love is patient [long-suffering, forbearing], love is kind [acts benevolently, useful]. It does not envy, it does not boast, it is not proud [puffed up, inflated].","It is not rude [unbecoming, unseemly], it is not self-seeking, it is not easily angered [provoked, exasperated], it keeps no account [does not reckon, impute] of wrongs.","Love takes no pleasure in evil [injustice, unrighteousness, wrong], but rejoices in the truth [what is true].","It bears [covers, patiently endures] all things, believes all things, hopes [expects, confidently trusts] all things, endures [remains under, bears patiently] all things.","Love never fails [falls away, drops off]. But where there are prophecies, they will cease [be done away, abolished]; where there are tongues, they will be restrained [stopped, brought to an end]; where there is knowledge, it will be dismissed.","For we know [perceive, have knowledge] in part and we prophesy in part,","but when the perfect [complete, full-grown] comes, the partial passes away [is done away, rendered useless].","When I was a child, I talked like a child, I thought [kept on thinking, minding] like a child, I reasoned like a child. When I became a man, I set aside [put away, done away] childish ways.","Now we see but a dim reflection [obscureness, enigma] as in a mirror; then we shall see face to face. Now I know in part; then I shall know fully [recognize, become fully acquainted], even as I am fully known.","And now these three remain [abide, continue, endure]: faith, hope [confident expectation], and love; but the greatest of these is love [affection, benevolence]."],["Earnestly pursue [keep on following after] love [affection, benevolence] and eagerly desire [keep on earnestly desiring] spiritual gifts, especially the gift of prophecy.","For he who speaks in a tongue does not speak to men, but to God. Indeed, no one understands him; he utters mysteries [secrets] in the Spirit.","But he who prophesies speaks to men for their edification [building up], encouragement [exhortation, entreaty], and comfort [consolation].","The one who speaks in a tongue edifies [builds up] himself, but the one who prophesies edifies the church [assembly].","I wish that all of you could speak in tongues, but I would rather have you prophesy. He who prophesies is greater than one who speaks in tongues, unless he interprets [explains thoroughly, translates] so that the church may be edified.","Now, brothers, if I come to you speaking in tongues, how will I benefit [profit, be useful to] you, unless I bring you some revelation [disclosure, unveiling] or knowledge or prophecy or teaching [instruction]?","Even in the case of lifeless [without life, inanimate] instruments, such as the flute or harp, how will anyone recognize the tune they are playing unless the notes are distinct [varied, distinguished]?","Again, if the trumpet sounds a muffled [indistinct, uncertain] call, who will prepare for battle?","So it is with you. Unless you speak intelligible [significant, easy to understand] words with your tongue, how will anyone know what you are saying? You will just be speaking into the air.","Assuredly, there are many different languages in the world, yet none of them is without meaning [voiceless, mute].","If, then, I do not know the meaning of someone’s language, I am a foreigner [barbarian] to the speaker, and he is a foreigner to me.","It is the same with you. Since you are eager [zealous] to have spiritual gifts, strive [keep on seeking] to excel [abound, superabound] in gifts that build up the church.","Therefore, the one who speaks in a tongue should pray that he may interpret.","For if I pray in a tongue, my spirit prays, but my mind [understanding, intellect] is unfruitful [barren, without fruit].","What then shall I do? I will pray with my spirit, but I will also pray with my mind. I will sing [make melody] with my spirit, but I will also sing with my mind.","Otherwise, if you speak a blessing in spirit, how can someone who is uninstructed [unlearned, a private person] say “Amen” to your thanksgiving [grateful language, thanks], since he does not know what you are saying?","You may be giving thanks well enough, but the other one is not edified [built up].","I thank God that I speak in tongues more than all of you.","But in the church, I would rather speak five coherent words to instruct [teach, inform] others than ten thousand words in a tongue.","Brothers, stop thinking [understanding] like children. In regard to evil [malice, wickedness] be infants, but in your thinking be mature [complete, full-grown].","It is written in the Law: “By strange tongues and foreign lips I will speak to this people, but even then they will not listen [hear, give heed] to Me, says the Lord.”","Tongues, then, are a sign [token, indication], not for believers, but for unbelievers [those without faith]. Prophecy, however, is for believers, not for unbelievers.","So if the whole church comes together and everyone speaks in tongues, and some who are uninstructed or some unbelievers come in, will they not say that you are out of your minds [raving, mad]?","But if an unbeliever or uninstructed person comes in while everyone is prophesying, he will be convicted [rebuked, convinced] and called to account [examined, scrutinized] by all,","and the secrets [hidden things] of his heart will be made known [manifest, apparent]. So he will fall facedown and worship [bow down, prostrate himself] God, proclaiming, “God is truly among you!”","What then shall we say, brothers? When you come together, everyone has a psalm or a teaching, a revelation [disclosure, unveiling], a tongue, or an interpretation. All of these must be done to build up [edification] the church.","If anyone speaks in a tongue, two, or at most three, should speak in turn, and someone must interpret.","But if there is no interpreter, he should remain silent [keep silent] in the church and speak only to himself and God.","Two or three prophets should speak, and the others should weigh carefully [discern, judge thoroughly] what is said.","And if a revelation [is disclosed, revealed] comes to someone who is seated, the first speaker should stop.","For you can all prophesy in turn so that everyone may be instructed [learn] and encouraged [comforted, exhorted].","The spirits of prophets are subject [subordinate, under control] to prophets.","For God is not a God of disorder [instability, confusion], but of peace [quietness, rest]—as in all the churches of the saints [holy ones].","Women are to be silent in the churches. They are not permitted to speak, but must be in submission [subordination, obedience], as the law says.","If they wish to inquire [learn] about something, they are to ask their own husbands at home; for it is dishonorable [shameful, base] for a woman to speak in the church.","Did the word of God originate with you? Or are you the only ones it has reached [arrived, come]?","If anyone considers himself a prophet or spiritual person, let him acknowledge [recognize, fully know] that what I am writing you is the Lord’s command [commandment, authoritative precept].","But if anyone ignores [does not know, disregards] this, he himself will be ignored.","So, my brothers, be eager [keep on earnestly desiring] to prophesy, and do not forbid [hinder, prevent] speaking in tongues.","But everything must be done in a proper and orderly [in regular arrangement] manner."],["Now, brothers, I want to remind you of the gospel [good news] I preached to you, which you received [took to yourselves], and in which you stand firm [and continue standing].","By this gospel you are saved [being saved, delivered], if you hold firmly [keep holding fast] to the word I preached to you. Otherwise, you have believed in vain.","For what I received I passed on [delivered, entrusted] to you as of first importance: that Christ died for our sins [offenses, missing the mark] according to the Scriptures,","that He was buried, that He was raised [and remains raised] on the third day according to the Scriptures,","and that He appeared to Cephas and then to the Twelve.","After that, He appeared to more than five hundred brothers at once, most of whom are still living, though some have fallen asleep [died, slumbered].","Then He appeared to James, then to all the apostles.","And last of all He appeared to me also, as to one of untimely birth [born out of due time].","For I am the least of the apostles and am unworthy [not fit, not sufficient] to be called an apostle, because I persecuted [pursued] the church of God.","But by the grace [favor, graciousness] of God I am what I am, and His grace to me was not in vain [empty]. No, I worked harder [toiled, labored to weariness] than all of them—yet not I, but the grace of God that was with me.","Whether, then, it was I or they, this is what we preach [proclaim, herald], and this is what you believed.","But if it is preached that Christ has been raised from the dead, how can some of you say that there is no resurrection [standing up again] of the dead?","If there is no resurrection of the dead, then not even Christ has been raised.","And if Christ has not been raised, our preaching is worthless [empty, void], and so is your faith [conviction, belief].","In that case, we are also exposed as false witnesses [bearers of untrue testimony] about God. For we have testified [borne witness] about God that He raised Christ from the dead, but He did not raise Him if in fact the dead are not raised.","For if the dead are not raised, then not even Christ has been raised.","And if Christ has not been raised, your faith is futile [empty, profitless]; you are still in your sins.","Then those also who have fallen asleep in Christ have perished [been fully destroyed, lost].","If our hope [have confidently expected] in Christ is for this life alone, we are to be pitied [pitiable, miserable] more than all men.","But Christ has indeed been raised from the dead, the firstfruits [beginning of the harvest offering] of those who have fallen asleep.","For since death came through a man, the resurrection of the dead comes also through a man.","For as in Adam all die, so in Christ all will be made alive [given life, quickened].","But each in his own turn [order, rank]: Christ the firstfruits; then at His coming [presence, arrival], those who belong to Him.","Then the end will come, when He hands over the kingdom [royal rule, reign] to God the Father after He has destroyed [abolished, rendered powerless] all dominion [rule, principality], authority, and power.","For He must reign [rule as king] until He has put all His enemies under His feet.","The last enemy to be destroyed [abolished, made idle] is death.","For “God has put everything under [subjected, subordinated] His feet.” Now when it says that everything has been put under Him, this clearly does not include the One who put everything under Him.","And when all things have been subjected to Him, then the Son Himself will be made subject to Him who put all things under Him, so that God may be all in all.","If these things are not so, what will those do who are baptized for the dead? If the dead are not raised at all, why are people baptized for them?","And why do we endanger ourselves [stand in peril] every hour?","I face death [keep on dying] every day, brothers, as surely as I boast [glorying, rejoicing] about you in Christ Jesus our Lord.","If I fought wild beasts in Ephesus for human motives, what did I gain? If the dead are not raised, “Let us eat and drink, for tomorrow we die.”","Do not be deceived [led astray]: “Bad company corrupts [spoils, ruins] good character [moral habits].”","Sober up [awake, rouse yourselves] as you ought, and stop sinning [missing the mark]; for some of you are ignorant [without knowledge] of God. I say this to your shame.","But someone will ask, “How are the dead raised? With what kind of body will they come?”","You fool! What you sow does not come to life [made alive, quickened] unless it dies.","And what you sow is not the body that will be, but just a seed [bare kernel], perhaps of wheat or something else.","But God gives it a body as He has designed [willed, chosen], and to each kind of seed He gives its own body.","Not all flesh is the same: Men have one kind of flesh, animals have another, birds another, and fish another.","There are also heavenly bodies and earthly bodies. But the splendor [glory, brightness] of the heavenly bodies is of one degree, and the splendor of the earthly bodies is of another.","The sun has one degree of splendor, the moon another, and the stars another; and star differs from star in splendor.","So will it be with the resurrection of the dead: What is sown is perishable [decay, corruption]; it is raised imperishable [incorruption, unending existence].","It is sown in dishonor [shame, indignity]; it is raised in glory [splendor, honor]. It is sown in weakness; it is raised in power [might, force].","It is sown a natural [animate, of the soul-life] body; it is raised a spiritual [non-fleshly, supernatural] body. If there is a natural body, there is also a spiritual body.","So it is written: “The first man Adam became a living [alive, having life] being;” the last Adam a life-giving [making alive] spirit.","The spiritual, however, was not first, but the natural, and then the spiritual.","The first man was of the dust [soil-like, earthy] of the earth, the second man from heaven.","As was the earthly man, so also are those who are of the earth; and as is the heavenly man, so also are those who are of heaven.","And just as we have borne the likeness [image] of the earthly man, so also shall we bear the likeness of the heavenly man.","Now I declare to you, brothers, that flesh and blood cannot inherit [be heirs to] the kingdom of God, nor does the perishable inherit the imperishable [incorruptibility].","Listen, I tell you a mystery [secret]: We will not all sleep, but we will all be changed [made different]—","in an instant [indivisible moment], in the twinkling of an eye, at the last trumpet. For the trumpet will sound, the dead will be raised imperishable [undecaying, incorruptible], and we will be changed.","For the perishable must be clothed [invested, arrayed] with the imperishable, and the mortal [liable to die] with immortality [deathlessness].","When the perishable has been clothed with the imperishable and the mortal with immortality, then the saying that is written will come to pass: “Death has been swallowed up [devoured] in victory [triumph, conquest].”","“Where, O Death, is your victory? Where, O Death, is your sting [point, prick]?”","The sting of death is sin [missing the mark], and the power [force, strength] of sin is the law.","But thanks be to God, who gives us the victory [triumph, conquest] through our Lord Jesus Christ!","Therefore, my beloved brothers, be steadfast [settled, firmly seated] and immovable. Always excel [keep on abounding] in the work of the Lord, because you know that your labor [toil, weariness] in the Lord is not in vain."],["Now about the collection [contribution] for the saints [holy ones], you are to do as I directed [arranged, instructed] the churches of Galatia:","On the first day of every week, each of you should set aside [keep on laying aside] a portion of his income [as he prospers], saving it up [storing up, treasuring], so that when I come no collections will be needed.","Then, on my arrival, I will send letters with those you recommend [approve after testing] to carry your gift [gracious gift, benefit] to Jerusalem.","And if it is advisable [fitting, worthwhile] for me to go also, they can travel with me.","After I go through Macedonia, however, I will come to you; for I will be going through Macedonia.","Perhaps I will stay with you awhile, or even spend the winter, so that you can help me on my journey [send forward, escort], wherever I go.","For I do not want to see you now only in passing; I hope [confidently expect] to spend some time with you, if the Lord permits [allows].","But I will stay in Ephesus until Pentecost,","because a great door for effective [active, powerful] work has opened to me, even though many oppose [are adversaries] me.","If Timothy comes, see to it that he has nothing to fear while he is with you, for he is doing the work of the Lord, just as I am.","No one, then, should treat him with contempt [disdain, despising]. Send him on his way in peace [quietness, rest] so that he can return to me, for I am expecting [waiting for] him along with the brothers.","Now about our brother Apollos: I strongly urged [entreated, exhorted] him to go to you with the brothers. He was not at all inclined [his will, desire] to go now, but he will go when he has the opportunity.","Be on the alert [keep on watching, stay awake]. Stand firm [keep standing fast, persevere] in the faith. Be men of courage. Be strong [keep being strengthened].","Do everything in love [affection, benevolence].","You know that Stephanas and his household were the first converts [firstfruits] in Achaia, and they have devoted [appointed, set] themselves to the service [ministry, attendance] of the saints. Now I urge you, brothers,","to submit [be subject, subordinate] to such as these, and to every fellow worker and laborer [one who toils].","I am glad that Stephanas, Fortunatus, and Achaicus have arrived, because they have supplied [filled up] what was lacking from you.","For they refreshed [gave rest to] my spirit and yours as well. Show your appreciation [recognize, acknowledge], therefore, to such men.","The churches in the province of Asia send you greetings. Aquila and Prisca greet you warmly in the Lord, and so does the church that meets at their house.","All the brothers here send you greetings. Greet one another with a holy [sacred, pure] kiss.","This greeting is in my own hand—Paul.","If anyone does not love [have fond affection for] the Lord, let him be under a curse [ban, anathema]. Come, O Lord!","The grace [favor, graciousness] of the Lord Jesus be with you.","My love [affection, benevolence] be with all of you in Christ Jesus. Amen."]]);
